License Plate Recognition System
Abstract
License Plate Recognition (LPR) is an image-processing application used to automatically detect and recognize vehicle registration numbers from images or videos. This system helps in traffic monitoring, parking management, toll collection, and security surveillance. The project uses computer vision and Optical Character Recognition (OCR) techniques to extract text from vehicle number plates.
Introduction
With the increase in the number of vehicles, manual monitoring of license plates has become difficult. License Plate Recognition automates this process by detecting the number plate from an image and converting the plate characters into digital text. The system improves accuracy and reduces human effort.
Objectives
Detect vehicle number plates automatically.
Extract characters from the detected plate.
Convert image data into readable text.
Improve traffic and parking management systems.
Software Requirements
Python 3.x
OpenCV
EasyOCR
NumPy
Hardware Requirements
Computer/Laptop
Webcam or Camera (optional)
Minimum 4 GB RAM
Methodology
Step 1: Image Acquisition
Capture or upload a vehicle image containing a license plate.
Step 2: Preprocessing
Convert the image into a suitable format using image processing techniques.
Step 3: Plate Detection
Locate the number plate region from the vehicle image.
Step 4: Character Recognition
Apply OCR to identify and extract the characters present on the license plate.
Step 5: Output Display
Display the detected license plate number on the screen.import cv2
import easyocr

# Initialize OCR Reader
reader = easyocr.Reader(['en'])

# Load Image
image = cv2.imread('car.jpg')

# Read Text
results = reader.readtext(image)

# Display Detected Text
for result in results:
    print("Detected Plate Number:", result[1])

cv2.imshow("Vehicle Image", image)
cv2.waitKey(0)
cv2.destroyAllWindows()Applications
